@startuml Contact_Data_Model
' Edison UPM - Contact options data model (Sprint 2, task 2.3.7, US 2.3 Contact Options)
' Design proposal. Replaces the single free-text column ideas.contact (VARCHAR 2000)
' from branch feature/contact with structured, validated contact options, each with
' its own audience, so founders' emails and phones are not public by default.

title Edison UPM - Contact Data Model (Sprint 2)

skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam nodesep 80
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F1F1F1
  BorderColor #555555
  AttributeFontSize 11
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #333333
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #555555
}
hide circle
hide empty methods

' ================= CLASS MODEL (backend) =================
package "Class model (backend)" as CLASSES {

  class Idea <<Sprint 1>> {
    id : UUID
    status : IdeaStatus
    visibility : Visibility
    .. other attributes omitted ..
    contactOptions : List<ContactOption> {0..5}
  }

  class User <<Sprint 1>> {
    id : UUID
    role : UserRole
  }

  class ContactOption <<new>> {
    id : UUID
    type : ContactType
    value : String {length <= 254, validated by type}
    label : String [0..1] {length <= 40}
    audience : ContactAudience
    displayOrder : Integer
    createdAt : DateTime
    updatedAt : DateTime [0..1]
  }

  enum ContactType {
    EMAIL = "Email"
    LINKEDIN = "LinkedIn"
    WEBSITE = "Website"
    PHONE = "Phone"
  }

  enum ContactAudience {
    ALL_VIEWERS = "Everyone who can see the idea"
    SIGNED_IN = "Signed-in users"
    INVESTORS = "Investors only"
  }

  Idea "1" *-down- "0..5" ContactOption : contactOptions
  Idea "0..*" -up-> "1" User : founder
  ContactOption --> "1" ContactType : type
  ContactOption --> "1" ContactAudience : audience

  note as NRules
    <b>Rules (checked by IdeaService)</b>
    Only the founder adds, edits, removes
    or reorders contact options.
    Max. 5 per idea; the same type + value
    cannot be repeated.
    Optional: an idea can be published
    with no contact options.
    Default audience: SIGNED_IN.
  end note

  note as NValidation
    <b>Validation of value by type</b>
    EMAIL: valid e-mail address
    LINKEDIN: https://(www.)linkedin.com/...
    WEBSITE: HTTP or HTTPS URL
    PHONE: international format, e.g.
    +34 600 123 456 (E.164 when stored)
  end note

  NRules -[hidden]down- NValidation
}

' ================= ER MODEL (MySQL) =================
package "ER model (MySQL)" as TABLES {

  class ideas <<table>> {
    id : CHAR(36) <<PK>>
    founder_id : CHAR(36) <<FK>>
    .. other columns omitted ..
  }

  class idea_contact_options <<table, new>> {
    id : CHAR(36) <<PK>>
    idea_id : CHAR(36) <<FK>>
    type : VARCHAR(20)
    value : VARCHAR(254)
    label : VARCHAR(40) NULL
    audience : VARCHAR(20)
    display_order : INT
    created_at : DATETIME(6)
    updated_at : DATETIME(6) NULL
    --
    UNIQUE (idea_id, type, value)
    CHECK type IN (EMAIL, LINKEDIN, WEBSITE, PHONE)
    CHECK audience IN (ALL_VIEWERS, SIGNED_IN, INVESTORS)
  }

  ideas "1" *-- "0..*" idea_contact_options : ON DELETE CASCADE
}

ContactOption .down.> idea_contact_options : <<persisted in>>

note bottom of idea_contact_options
  The max. of 5 options per idea is
  checked by the backend, not the DB.
  Replaces ideas.contact VARCHAR(2000)
  from branch feature/contact.
end note

note right of ContactAudience
  <b>Who sees each option</b> (API responses)
  The founder always sees all of them.
  Others only get the options whose audience
  they match; the rest are left out of the
  response (not just hidden in the UI).
  Investors see only PUBLIC ideas, so
  INVESTORS options appear on PUBLIC ideas.
end note
@enduml
